<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The mark: a ring with a gap, and the dot sitting in the gap.

  WHY THIS SHAPE

  The app answers one question — what comes round next — and the ring is that
  question drawn. It is open rather than closed because a closed circle is a
  finished thing, and nothing this app tracks is ever finished; it comes back.
  The dot is the moment it comes back, sitting exactly in the break.

  It is also the ○ that every row on the home screen begins with, made large.
  An icon that is a piece of the app is one you recognise on the way in.

  GEOMETRY, SO IT CAN BE CHANGED WITHOUT GUESSING

  An adaptive icon is drawn on a 108 by 108 canvas of which only the middle 66
  is guaranteed to survive the launcher's mask — the rest can be cropped to a
  circle, a squircle or a rounded square depending on the phone. So everything
  here stays inside a circle of radius 33 around the centre at 54,54.

    ring    centre 54,54   radius 26   stroke 8   outer edge at 30
    gap     70 degrees wide, centred on the top
    dot     centre 54,28   radius 5.5  topmost point at 31.5 from centre

  The arc runs clockwise from the right-hand side of the gap all the way round
  to the left-hand side, which is 290 degrees, hence the large-arc flag.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:pathData="M68.91,32.70 A26,26 0 1 1 39.09,32.70"
        android:strokeColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:strokeWidth="8"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000" />
    <path
        android:pathData="M48.5,28 a5.5,5.5 0 1,0 11,0 a5.5,5.5 0 1,0 -11,0"
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF" />
</vector>